44-The Department requested public comment regarding the appropriate use of the authority conferred by the statute upon the Attorney General to expand the class of aliens subject to expedited removal. Most commenters commended the Department on its decision not to apply at this time the expedited removal provisions to aliens in the United States who have not been admitted or paroled and who cannot establish continuous physical presence in the United States for the previous two years. At this time, the Department will apply the provisions only to ‘‘arriving aliens,’’ as defined in § 1.1(q). The Department acknowledges that application of the expedited removal provisions to aliens already in the United States will involve more complex determinations of fact and will be more difficult to manage, and therefore wishes to gain insight and experience by initially applying these new provisions on a more limited and controlled basis.
